      "problem": "Find the value of $f(t)=(t+1)^{2}-2(t+1)$ at $t=-2.$",
      "worked_solution": "We substitute $t=-2$ into the function definition and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(t+1)^{2}-2(t+1) \\\\ f(-2) & =(-2+1)^{2}-2(-2+1) \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}-2(-1) \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
